engine/lib/hand-glyphs.js — glyph strokes of the Hershey vector fonts.

The Hershey Fonts were originally created by Dr. A. V. Hershey while working at the U. S. National Bureau of Standards
(NBS report "Calligraphy for Computers", 1967). As a work of the U.S. Government the glyph data is in the public domain;
the customary request of its distributors is that this origin be acknowledged, which this file does.

The coordinates were read out of the copy of the tables built into R (grDevices vfont, by way of GNU plotutils) with
scripts/hand_glyphs.R and scripts/hand_glyphs.py; no R or plotutils code is included. Faces used: Script (Latin
cursive), Complex Cyrillic (oblique), Simplex Roman (sans).
